  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Greeting**: rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n- **Sally Goodin**: back after 70 archived shows (673 days) [5]\n- **Letter Edged In Black**: back after 60 archived shows (650 days); rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n- **The Night That The Lights Went Out In Georgia**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Wharf Rat**: rare: 10 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2021-12-11** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 137 min [1]\n- **billystrings2021-12-11.bstrings**: source not stated; 19 songs; 138 min [2]\n- **billystrings2021-12-11.tfunk.tk60.mitchell.flac2448**: source not stated; 19 songs; 138 min [3]\n- **billystrings2021-12-11.mk41**: source not stated; 19 songs; 138 min [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Band lineup listed: William Apostle on acoustic guitar, Royal Masat bass, Jarrod Walker mandolin, and Billy Falling banjo, all singing [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2021-12-11**: taped by Z-Man; transferred by Z-Man; source: Schoeps CCM4V'S>Lunatec V2>Sound Devices 722 (24/44.1) [1]. Also: Captured with Schoeps CCM4V microphones into a Lunatec V2 preamp, then a Sound Devices 722 recorder at 24-bit/44.1kHz; Z-Man recorded and seeded it, with the mics clamped to the mezzanine rail; it was edited in Sound Forge and converted to 16-bit FLAC [1]\n- **billystrings2021-12-11.bstrings**: taped by David Dyche; transferred by David Dyche; source: Neumann 150’s > (Clamped To The Rail Of The Mezzanine) V-3 > Sound Devices 744 24/96 [2]\n- **billystrings2021-12-11.tfunk.tk60.mitchell.flac2448**: taped by Jeff Mitchell; transferred by Jeff Mitchell; source: AKG CK1 > Nbob Actives > Audioroot Femto > Zoom F8n > SDXC > Samplitude Pro X5 > dBpoweramp > Foobar Live Show Tagger > Traders Little Helper [3]\n- **billystrings2021-12-11.mk41**: taped by davidpuddy; source: Schoeps mk41 > nbob actives > baby nbox > Mixpre 6ii (32bit/48khz) [4]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings The Eastern - Atlanta, GA - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/show/the-eastern-atlanta-ga/) [6]",
